WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.761
You've got a planner, or a notebook
you made, and an e-ink tablet.

2
00:00:03.889 --> 00:00:06.979
There are two ways onto it,
for two different jobs.

3
00:00:07.038 --> 00:00:11.998
I'm starting from the 2026 Planner
preset, so there's no design work.

4
00:00:12.208 --> 00:00:14.478
The first is the linked PDF.

5
00:00:14.555 --> 00:00:19.996
Export PDF, from episode one,
makes the whole planner one file:

6
00:00:19.996 --> 00:00:23.355
all 1,368 pages, every link working.

7
00:00:23.409 --> 00:00:26.581
You open it on the tablet
and write on its pages.

8
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.900
Its pages come out at the size
of the variant you're on.

9
00:00:29.961 --> 00:00:34.281
This planner has one, Default,
sized for a reMarkable Paper Pro.

10
00:00:34.347 --> 00:00:39.037
A tablet of another shape needs its
own variant: that's episode nine.

11
00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:43.874
The second is note templates: page
designs your tablet draws behind your

12
00:00:43.874 --> 00:00:45.987
handwriting, in any notebook.

13
00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:51.129
Each page becomes an image at the
tablet's exact pixel size, with no links.

14
00:00:51.335 --> 00:00:55.515
So: the PDF when you want the
planner itself, dated and linked.

15
00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:59.607
Templates when you want its page
designs in the tablet's own notebooks.

16
00:00:59.812 --> 00:01:02.952
The picker lists pages
first, grouped by template.

17
00:01:03.046 --> 00:01:07.446
Each group starts with its first page
ticked, so you get one of each design.

18
00:01:07.747 --> 00:01:14.347
That's the usual want: one page of each
design, not 365 copies of the Day View.

19
00:01:14.432 --> 00:01:17.502
I don't need the year page,
so none clears its group.

20
00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:20.288
Search reaches the pages
tucked under more.

21
00:01:20.342 --> 00:01:22.552
I'd like December's month page too.

22
00:01:22.672 --> 00:01:25.972
In the search box, Escape
clears it and keeps the tick.

23
00:01:26.003 --> 00:01:28.623
Anywhere else, Escape closes the picker.

24
00:01:28.828 --> 00:01:34.038
One catch: a template is a picture of a
page, so a dated page keeps its date.

25
00:01:34.169 --> 00:01:38.149
Use December's, and every page
you write on says December.

26
00:01:38.186 --> 00:01:43.269
So I'll keep the note and to-do pages, which
suit any day, and none clears the rest.

27
00:01:43.358 --> 00:01:48.208
That includes the journal and daily notes
pages: their top bar shows the month.

28
00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:59.818
Below the pages, Rescale to lists one
option per screen, grouped by brand.

29
00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.240
Until one is ticked, Export waits.

30
00:02:02.326 --> 00:02:03.926
I'll tick Paper Pure.

31
00:02:04.031 --> 00:02:08.661
The reMarkable 2 under it has the same
screen, so it gets the same file.

32
00:02:08.866 --> 00:02:13.219
Color screens get color templates;
every other model gets grey,

33
00:02:13.219 --> 00:02:16.647
converted like episode
six's greyscale export.

34
00:02:16.774 --> 00:02:21.264
So the Paper Pure comes out grey, and
the Boox Note Air C keeps its color.

35
00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:23.785
Force greyscale makes them all grey.

36
00:02:23.869 --> 00:02:28.469
And ticking the Boox brought up a new
box: Also include a PDF template.

37
00:02:28.675 --> 00:02:31.838
It puts your pages in one
PDF beside the images,

38
00:02:31.838 --> 00:02:37.095
with the links between them still working.
reMarkable folders never get one.

39
00:02:37.151 --> 00:02:39.691
I'll add a Supernote Manta, and tick it.

40
00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:48.781
The line at the bottom keeps count: two
pages on three devices, six templates.

41
00:02:48.908 --> 00:02:54.107
The ceiling is 400 images per export,
about what a phone browser can zip.

42
00:02:54.316 --> 00:02:58.051
Ticking all on the Day View
asks for every day of the year:

43
00:02:58.051 --> 00:03:00.390
too many files, and Export waits.

44
00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.270
Then none clears the group,
and we're back under.

45
00:03:03.872 --> 00:03:08.892
Export draws every image right here in the
browser, and the line counts them off.

46
00:03:08.953 --> 00:03:11.733
Cancel would stop it,
with nothing downloaded.

47
00:03:11.837 --> 00:03:15.384
Your devices and both boxes
are remembered for next time;

48
00:03:15.384 --> 00:03:17.314
the page ticks start fresh.

49
00:03:18.029 --> 00:03:22.920
One zip, one folder per model, each
laid out the way that device expects.

50
00:03:23.018 --> 00:03:27.309
That's png and methods for the
reMarkable, MyStyle for the Manta,

51
00:03:27.309 --> 00:03:29.540
and noteTemplate for the Boox.

52
00:03:29.758 --> 00:03:34.702
Here's the Paper Pure's to-do
page: 1404 × 1872 pixels,

53
00:03:34.702 --> 00:03:38.098
the tablet's exact screen, in grey.

54
00:03:38.852 --> 00:03:41.542
Each folder has an INSTALL.txt.

55
00:03:41.597 --> 00:03:46.368
Here's the Manta's: connect by USB,
copy the MyStyle folder across,

56
00:03:46.368 --> 00:03:50.037
then pick a page under
Templates, Customization.

57
00:03:50.243 --> 00:03:54.253
That copying is yours to do: the
app never touches your tablet.

58
00:03:54.398 --> 00:03:59.288
And reMarkable is the hard one, with no
official way to add templates at all.

59
00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:06.283
So its INSTALL.txt opens with a warning:
both routes need SSH, at your own risk.

60
00:04:06.319 --> 00:04:10.776
Start with methods: line drawings
that survive software updates;

61
00:04:10.776 --> 00:04:14.369
the PNGs look exact, but
an update removes them.

62
00:04:14.481 --> 00:04:18.827
On a Paper Pro, getting SSH
at all means a factory reset.

63
00:04:18.889 --> 00:04:21.099
The linked PDF needs none of that.

64
00:04:21.304 --> 00:04:23.604
That's both ways onto your tablet.

65
00:04:23.742 --> 00:04:27.332
Next time: keeping your work safe,
in the browser and out of it.
